WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.190
This slide summarizes the normalization progression
First

00:00:05.216 --> 00:00:07.822
Normal Form removes repeating groups and list-like

00:00:07.835 --> 00:00:10.348
values so each field represents one value

00:00:12.087 --> 00:00:15.034
Second Normal Form handles partial dependencies when

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:18.168
a composite key is involved Facts that

00:00:18.181 --> 00:00:19.813
depend on only part of that key

00:00:19.826 --> 00:00:24.411
move elsewhere Third Normal Form removes transitive

00:00:24.437 --> 00:00:26.832
dependencies so non-key facts are stored with

00:00:26.858 --> 00:00:30.741
the entity that actually determines them A

00:00:30.767 --> 00:00:32.754
fast diagnostic is to ask how many

00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:35.070
rows must change when one fact changes

00:00:36.794 --> 00:00:39.215
If changing a patient's name requires updating

00:00:39.228 --> 00:00:42.662
many appointment-service rows patient information is
probably

00:00:42.688 --> 00:00:45.917
stored in the wrong place In a

00:00:45.943 --> 00:00:48.996
well-designed operational schema one patient fact
should

00:00:49.022 --> 00:00:51.325
usually be updated in one patient row
